<title>NORWAY: TABLE - AKER RGI H1 RESULT PER DIVISION.</title>
<headline>TABLE - AKER RGI H1 RESULT PER DIVISION.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Operating result per division at Aker RGI ASA for the six months to June 30.</p>
<p>					   (millions of NOK unless stated)</p>
<p> Scancem (SEK million)			N/A	vs	677 *</p>
<p> Aker Maritime				   96	vs	151</p>
<p>Norway Seafoods</p>
<p> (incl. Frionor)			minus 129	vs	 58 **</p>
<p> Legend Properties (estimate)     minus  10	vs	N/A</p>
<p> Constructor Group			     22	vs	  5</p>
<p> Langsten					  10	vs	 48</p>
<p> Brattvaag Industrier			  10	vs minus  3</p>
<p> Brooks					    15	vs	  4</p>
<p> Libris EMO			     minus  11	vs minus  4</p>
<p> Atlas Stord			    minus  18	vs minus 22</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>* - Swedish/Norwegian building materials group Scancem AB is due to post first-half results on August 26. Aker RGI said it estimated its profits from the group at 80 million Swedish crowns.</p>
<p>** - Norway Seafoods booked extraordinary costs of 150 million crowns in the second quarter and posted a pre-tax loss of 313 million crowns.</p>
<p>AKER RGI ASA was established last year after engineering and construction group AKER ASA merged with investment company Resource Group International (RGI). Comparative 1996 figures are calculated on a pro forma basis.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
